      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-145559",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be discrete random variables with the joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ shown below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y = 2$ | $Y = 4$ | $Y = 6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X = 2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nIf $F(x, y)$ is the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y$, find $F(2, 4)$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
